   260	// Corner sign vector for offset o ∈ {0,1}³ (the ONE sign function D, G, and diag(A) share).

 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	// U4 free surface + constraint bubble (plan 2026-06-09-001 U4 / KTD-6).
     2	//
     3	// ================================ POCKET DETECTION ============================================
     4	// Air cells (cell_meta.w = CELL_AIR after cell_classify: no fluid, center in-box, not inside a
     5	// solid) are flood-filled from the OPEN boundary: the topmost in-box cell layer is the
     6	// atmosphere (the box's side/bottom faces are sealed walls — air sealed against them is still
     7	// enclosed). The flood runs a scene-derived number of ping-pong relaxation sweeps (the grid
     8	// Manhattan diameter — `flood_sweeps_for` in mod.rs; labels in the pressure ping-pong buffers,
     9	// which cell_classify zeroed and pocket_mark re-zeroes) propagating the OUTSIDE label one
    10	// 6-neighbor step per sweep — uniform control flow, deterministic (read old / write new, never
    11	// racy in-place). The budget MUST cover the longest open-air path or genuinely-open air (e.g.
    12	// the deep V60 cup under its cone) is misread as one enclosed pocket and the bubble crushes the
    13	// standing water. Air cells still unlabeled afterwards are ENCLOSED: the
    14	// pocket. Single-pocket case (the pour cavity) per the plan: ALL enclosed air shares ONE
    15	// bubble — multi-pocket generalization is deferred scope.
    16	//
    17	// ================================ BUBBLE REPRESENTATION (KTD-6, pinned) =======================
    18	// ONE explicit Lagrange-multiplier scalar λ_b (bubble[0]); its value IS the pocket pressure.
    19	// Pocket cells are inserted into the SAME operator family as fluid rows: pocket_mark gives
    20	// them fill weight f = 1 and rhs = (0 − D v)/dt (no density relief — air), so
    21	//   * the COLUMN coupling is automatic: fluid rows and the projection gather pocket pressure
    22	//     through the one G = −Dᵀ (the pocket pressure acts on exactly the pocket-boundary faces
    23	//     — interior pocket nodes are massless, M̃⁻¹ = 0, and contribute nothing);
    24	//   * the ROW is the aggregate volume constraint Σ_{c∈pocket}(D u⁺)_c = 0 — the row sum of
    25	//     the per-cell rows, solved EXACTLY for the single unknown each relaxation step:
    26	//         λ_b ← λ_b + (Σ rhs_c − Σ (A p̃)_c) / (1ᵀ_pocket·A·1_pocket),
    27	//     where p̃ carries λ_b in the pocket slots and the denominator is the full aggregated
    28	//     quadratic form (cross terms between pocket cells included — computed as Σ(A·1_pocket)_c).
    29	// IDENTICAL REPRESENTATION AT BOTH LEVELS (the named failure is a coarse-only row the fine
    30	// sweeps relax away — and its mirror image): a bubble_fine step precedes EVERY fine Jacobi
    31	// sweep and jacobi_fine pins pocket slots to λ_b (Dirichlet copy of the multiplier); the
    32	// coarse error equation carries the bubble correction δλ_b (bubble[1]) the same way —
    33	// bubble_coarse precedes every coarse sweep, jacobi_coarse pins all-pocket coarse cells to
    34	// δλ_b, and prolong_add adds δλ_b (a scalar — its prolongation is exact) to the fine pocket
    35	// slots; the next bubble_fine folds λ_b ← λ_b + δλ_b before re-solving. p₀ = 0 doctrine:
    36	// pocket_mark zeroes λ_b and δλ_b every frame (no warm start). When the pocket is OPEN
    37	// (pre-enclosure — e.g. the jet annulus connects the cavity to outside air) there are no
    38	// pocket cells, the aggregated diagonal is 0, and λ_b is pinned inactive (p = 0 air).
    39	//
    40	// Tint discipline: bubble_fine/bubble_coarse run as ONE workgroup with a uniform trip count
    41	// (now over the COMPACTED pocket list, not all cells — U8 R9 fix) and predicated bodies, so
    42	// every workgroupBarrier() is in uniform control flow. All other passes use guard returns with
    43	// no barriers. Over-dispatch + early-out only (R8). Storage buffers per entry point ≤ 7 (see
    44	// MAX_STORAGE_BUFFERS_PER_ENTRY_POINT in mod.rs).
