The implementation confirms the current two-field projection is not a pure density constraint: density enters as a source/relief term in `cell_classify` and `pocket_mark`, while the solved operator remains a finite-iteration pressure projection on grid velocities. That supports the diagnosis, but it also shows the current solver already has a coarse correction and bubble multiplier, so “no global solve” language in the new doc needs a careful standard.
