   193	/// U4 flood-fill sweep budget: each sweep propagates the OUTSIDE label ONE 6-neighbor cell, so
   194	/// the budget must bound the longest open-air PATH (in cells) from any in-box air cell to the
   195	/// open top face. The earlier fixed 24 was a miscalculation: it covered the box gate scenes
   196	/// (tank air column ≈ 16 cells) but NOT the V60 cup, whose air path runs from the cup floor
   197	/// (y = -8) up through the cone apex and out the box top (y = +10) — ≈ 88 cells at the web
   198	/// spacing, plus the cup-radius lateral detour. With too few sweeps the cup/cone air never gets
   199	/// the OUTSIDE label, is misclassified as one enclosed POCKET, and the bubble constraint
   200	/// (λ ≈ −3000) crushes the standing water into the floor corner (the reported WaterOnly
   201	/// collapse). The budget is therefore the grid's MANHATTAN DIAMETER — (nx−1)+(ny−1)+(nz−1)
   202	/// cells — which upper-bounds any monotone 6-neighbor path on the grid regardless of geometry,
   203	/// rounded UP to even so the final labels land back in the pf_a slot (parity). It is scene-
   204	/// derived (a per-solver field), not a global constant, because the path length scales with the
   205	/// grid; cells beyond the budget still degrade conservatively (extra pocket members with
   206	/// massless nodes — zero row coupling).
   207	pub fn flood_sweeps_for(dims: [u32; 3]) -> u32 {
   208	    let diameter = (dims[0] - 1) + (dims[1] - 1) + (dims[2] - 1);
   209	    diameter + (diameter & 1) // round up to even
   210	}
