codex
XPBD does not compute buoyancy by differencing a smooth lambda grid. In `coupling.wgsl`, pressure is `max(-lambda, 0)` on water particles, and the grain/water impulse is accumulated through pairwise SPH-gradient kernels with explicit equal-and-opposite passes. That is close in spirit to a pressure force, but weaker than the doc’s “λ IS pore-pressure field; derive ∇λ exactly as XPBD” claim.
