     1	//! Twofield U8 — the R9 REAL-TIME GATE and the program close-out perf gates.
     2	//!
     3	//! This is the program's verdict. It measures the per-FRAME GPU cost of the FULL V60 saturated-
     4	//! pour scene at the PRE-REGISTERED 200k composition and asserts the hard, NO-FALLBACK gate:
     5	//! ≤ 33 ms/frame median on the reference device (Apple M5 — this machine). It also gates the
     6	//! linearity thesis (µs/Kparticle degradation 40k→200k within a factor PRE-REGISTERED here,
     7	//! before any 200k number is read into the threshold), the dispatch budget, the no-GPU-sync
     8	//! getter contract, the wasm32 target compile, and an offline grid-refinement (GCI) study.
     9	//!
    10	//! THE PER-FRAME COST. The per-pass `timestamp-query` sum (`profile().total_micros()`) captures
    11	//! ONE CFL substep; the deformable-bed frame runs `solid_substeps` of them (7 at the defaults),
    12	//! and every substep re-runs the full water+solid+pressure+surface pipeline (one shared `dt`).
    13	//! So the honest per-frame GPU cost is `substeps × timestamp_sum`; `dispatches_per_frame` already
    14	//! counts every substep, and the two are cross-checked here. This measures the real per-frame
    15	//! cost via device timestamps — NOT the many-frames-of-small-scenes-with-readbacks wall time that
    16	//! made `twofield_full`'s end-to-end gates run 35 min (a different thing entirely, see U7).
    17	//!
    18	//! Verdict posture (NO-FALLBACK program). If after the sanctioned honest cheap wins the 200k
    19	//! median does NOT meet 33 ms, the gate asserts the REAL number and goes RED — a failing-but-
    20	//! honest gate is the correct outcome of a bet that doesn't make budget. The breakdown printed
    21	//! by `examples/twofield_scaling` shows WHERE the time goes (the deferred CK-MPM / kernel-fusion
    22	//! levers' target). The gate is NOT loosened, the composition is NOT made cheaper, and the
    23	//! linearity factor is NOT tuned to the result.
