    74	
    75	## 5. Core abstractions (top-level only; implementations live in sub-module plans)
    76	
    77	### 5.1 The seam — `Solver` (solvers/base.rs)
    78	Every complete method implements one interface, so `engine`, `ui`, and `profiling` drive any solver uniformly. `step()` advances a **whole frame** — water, bed, internal coupling, extraction all happen inside, however that method prefers.
    79	
    80	Solver **descriptions are data, not trait code**: each solver's `SolverInfo` lives in the `engine/solvers.json` catalog (deserialized with serde) and is looked up by `SolverId`. Adding or amending a solver is a one-row data edit, so the trait carries no `descriptor()`.
    81	
    82	```rust
    83	// Deserialized from engine/solvers.json, keyed by SolverId.
    84	pub struct SolverInfo {
    85	    pub name: String,
    86	    pub paradigm: Paradigm,     // PositionBased | ForceBased | Hybrid
    87	    pub owns_grid: bool,
    88	    pub stability: Stability,   // Unconditional | CflLimited { c }
    89	}
    90	
    91	pub trait Solver {
    92	    fn build(scene: &Scene, mats: &Materials, cfg: &Config, gpu: &GpuContext) -> Self
    93	        where Self: Sized;
    94	    fn reset(&mut self, scene: &Scene);
    95	    fn step(&mut self, dt: f32, input: &EmissionInput); // one frame; internal substepping/coupling/extraction
    96	    fn particles(&self) -> ParticleBuffers;             // canonical particle buffers for rendering
    97	    fn metrics(&self) -> Metrics;                       // yield, TDS, drawdown, evenness
    98	    fn profile(&self) -> Profile;                       // per-pass GPU timestamps + dispatches-per-frame
    99	}
   100	```
   101	
   102	### 5.2 Orchestration — `engine/`
   103	- **Scene** — user-facing brew builder.
   104	- **Simulator** — holds **one** `Box<dyn Solver>`; runs the frame loop; feeds `EmissionInput` from `ui`/`emission`; pumps `particles()`/`metrics()`/`profile()` out to `ui` and `profiling`. Re-`build`s a different method (by `SolverId`) on the same `Scene` for the runtime solver-switch.
   105	- **State** — canonical snapshot decoupling solvers from rendering.
   106	
   107	### 5.3 Data flow
   108	`options` → `engine::Scene` → `Simulator` builds the active solver (from a registry keyed by config) → per frame: `vis` input → `solver.step` → `state`/`metrics`/`profile` → `vis` render + `profiler`. The shared spatial hash and `GpuContext` (`utils/`) are infrastructure used by solvers and the engine, owned by neither.
